Eco Sentry: Cognitive Edge Security


The Air-Gapped Cognitive Firewall


Traditional rule-based firewalls are too rigid for modern IoT networks, and sending logs to Cloud SIEMs incurs massive latency and cost.
The Solution: A local Vector Database (ChromaDB) acts as the memory core, continuously learning traffic baseline patterns. When an anomaly is detected, instead of just blocking it, a local TinyLlama agent analyzes the vector distance to explain why the packet is anomalous in plain English.

